amplitudes and quartic smooth pulses. Retain all scalar terms. There is no
determinant normalization, centering of eigenphases or projective distance.

Use 8 substeps per slot, degree N=320 and dyadic scale S=2^768. The exact
shifted coefficients and U recurrence are those derived in the chart note:

    A(z)=-i(K+a psi(x+z)P),
    (n+1)U_(n+1)=sum_(k=0)^min(4,n) A_k U_(n-k), U_0=I.

The previously derived majorant b(z)=7+32z+64z^2+128z^3+64z^4 remains a
valid, conservative U-only bound. At R=1/4, its integral is 773/240<4.
The scalar nonnegative coefficient majorant has value <81. At h=1/8,
the degree-320 operator tail is therefore delta=81/2^321.

Let Uhat be the exact product of the 192 truncated step polynomials. All
exact U-only segment propagators are unitary. Exact-suffix telescoping gives

    E_m<=delta sum_(k=0)^(m-1)(1+E_k)
        <=(1+delta)^m-1<=m delta exp(m delta)<2m delta.

Thus ||Uhat-U0||<=e0=384delta. Interval rounding is separately propagated
and encloses Uhat itself. All subsequent matrix powers use this same Uhat
